markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Schema Design for Simple Features

The unit wraps up by investigating how inconsistent field names and data types can lead to misinterpretation by both humans and AI in real-world datasets.

When the schema isn’t clear, different people (and systems) may read the same data in totally different ways.

## Same Fields, Different Interpretations

Look at how three different users interpret the same three fields: **Title, Experience, and Payment.**

<div style="max-width:600px; margin:0 auto; font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">

  <!-- Recent Graduate -->
  <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; margin-bottom:20px;">
    <div style="width:90px; height:90px; margin-right:-15px; z-index:2;">
      <img src="https://images.code.org/6354c6ebefb3eb450926f36bf280cf60-image-1781103946980.png"
           alt="Recent Graduate"
           style="width:90px; height:90px; border-radius:50%; border:3px solid #6b7280; object-fit:cover;">
    </div>

<div style="border:4px solid #6b7280; background:#f3f0ff; padding:12px 18px 12px 55px; width:420px;">
      <div style="font-weight:700; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:10px; color:#1f2937;">
        Recent Graduate
      </div>

  <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#374151;">
        <strong>Title:</strong> Desired job position
      </div>

  <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#374151;">
        <strong>Experience:</strong> Description of past roles
      </div>

  <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#374151;">
        <strong>Payment:</strong> Salary expectation
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Job Recruiter -->
  <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; margin-bottom:20px;">
    <div style="width:90px; height:90px; margin-right:-15px; z-index:2;">
      <img src="https://images.code.org/35971a04209b977d503d98f2132d306c-image-1781104130841.png"
           alt="Job Recruiter"
           style="width:90px; height:90px; border-radius:50%; border:3px solid #6b7280; object-fit:cover;">
    </div>

  <div style="border:4px solid #6b7280; background:#f2fcf7; padding:12px 18px 12px 55px; width:420px;">
      <div style="font-weight:700; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:10px; color:#1f2937;">
        Job Recruiter
      </div>

  <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#374151;">
        <strong>Title:</strong> Candidate recent job title
      </div>

  <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#374151;">
        <strong>Experience:</strong> Number of years in job
      </div>

  <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#374151;">
        <strong>Payment:</strong> Candidate's current salary
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- AI -->
  <div style="display:flex; align-items:center;">
    <div style="width:90px; height:90px; margin-right:-15px; z-index:2;">
      <img src="https://images.code.org/305f0a2fcd61b8bdcec59ddb6e76e590-image-1781104202730.png"
           alt="AI"
           style="width:90px; height:90px; border-radius:50%; border:3px solid #6b7280; object-fit:cover;">
    </div>

<div style="border:4px solid #6b7280; background:#f7f8fa; padding:12px 18px 12px 55px; width:420px;">
      <div style="font-weight:700; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:10px; color:#1f2937;">
        AI
      </div>

  <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#374151;">
        <strong>Title:</strong> A prefix like Dr. or Mrs.
      </div>

  <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#374151;">
        <strong>Experience:</strong> Product testimonial
      </div>

  <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#374151;">
        <strong>Payment:</strong> Credit card information
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

## Try It: Predict the Problem

Imagine an app uses the fields **Title**, **Experience**, and **Payment** to recommend job opportunities. What might go wrong?

<details style="background-color:#FFFFFF;padding:12px;margin-bottom:10px;border:1px solid #D9E3E5;border-radius:8px;box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
  <summary style="font-size:16px;font-weight:bold;">Title</summary>
  <div style="margin-top:14px;">
    <p style="font-size:13pt;line-height:1.45;margin:0;">
      The app may not know whether <strong>Title</strong> means a job title, a person’s title, or a project title. This could lead to incorrect filtering or confusing recommendations.
    </p>
  </div>
</details>

<details style="background-color:#FFFFFF;padding:12px;margin-bottom:10px;border:1px solid #D9E3E5;border-radius:8px;box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
  <summary style="font-size:16px;font-weight:bold;">Experience</summary>
  <div style="margin-top:14px;">
    <p style="font-size:13pt;line-height:1.45;margin:0;">
      The app may not know whether <strong>Experience</strong> means years in a job, past roles, or a review from someone else. This can make sorting and comparing data unreliable.
    </p>
  </div>
</details>

<details style="background-color:#FFFFFF;padding:12px;margin-bottom:10px;border:1px solid #D9E3E5;border-radius:8px;box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
  <summary style="font-size:16px;font-weight:bold;">Payment</summary>
  <div style="margin-top:14px;">
    <p style="font-size:13pt;line-height:1.45;margin:0;">
      The app may not know whether <strong>Payment</strong> means salary, a required fee, or credit card information. This could create privacy issues or misleading results.
    </p>
  </div>
</details>

<div style="background-color:#B7E0E5; border-radius:10px; padding:14px; margin:18px auto; max-width:85%;"> <p style="font-size:14pt; margin:0; line-height:135%;"> <strong>Big idea:</strong> A well-designed schema makes an app more trustworthy, scalable, and easier to maintain. </p> </div>

## Why This Matters

<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2, 1fr);gap:12px;margin:18px 0;">

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;">
    <p style="font-size:14pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0 0 8px 0;">🔎 Filters</p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt;line-height:1.4;margin:0;">Unclear fields can cause filters to miss or include the wrong items.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;">
    <p style="font-size:14pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0 0 8px 0;">🔢 Sorting</p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt;line-height:1.4;margin:0;">Numbers stored as text can sort incorrectly or compare unpredictably.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;">
    <p style="font-size:14pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0 0 8px 0;">🤖 AI Outputs</p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt;line-height:1.4;margin:0;">AI may generate confident responses from messy or unclear data.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;">
    <p style="font-size:14pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0 0 8px 0;">👤 Users</p>
    <p style="font-size:13pt;line-height:1.4;margin:0;">Labels that do not match user expectations can reduce trust.</p>
  </div>

</div>

These are things your students will have to consider when designing their **final project**. 






MARKDOWN
